KG42.register("slice-clusters-5edbc6c00e7c6bfdbbdc4285",{"id":"09-local_flexibility::v142-d-CL001","paper":"09-local_flexibility","title":"Procurement clearing and conditional payments for mutually exclusive service requests","source_pointer":"/clusters/31","node_ids":["COMP-60443ad093294c09","COMP-71b68181dcd38d38","COMP-459c6c859f38f049"],"rule_refs":["09-local_flexibility::v141-c-R001","09-local_flexibility::v141-c-R004","09-local_flexibility::v141-c-R005"],"visible_rule_refs":["09-local_flexibility::v141-c-R001","09-local_flexibility::v141-c-R004","09-local_flexibility::v141-c-R005"],"suppressed_rule_refs":[],"edges":[{"global_edge_id":"S-11e4eba59a6ce197","source":"COMP-60443ad093294c09","target":"COMP-71b68181dcd38d38","type":"links","assertion_ids":["09-local_flexibility::v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E001"],"rule_refs":["09-local_flexibility::v141-c-R004"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-f2fdfe453f0593e1","source":"COMP-60443ad093294c09","target":"COMP-459c6c859f38f049","type":"links","assertion_ids":["09-local_flexibility::v141-c-R005::E::v141-c-R005-E001"],"rule_refs":["09-local_flexibility::v141-c-R005"],"internal":false}],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"interface_annotations":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R001::x::v141-c-R001-X001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::clearing.local","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E12","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g02-e26"],"rationale":"The source places procurement clearing for mutually exclusive requests and the fee arrangements for purchased conditional services within the same market: the final activation cost is determined by the clearing result. This mapping links the two chains only when the purchased service is conditional, without interpreting the procurement-selection indicator as an activation indicator or presuming a specific pricing algorithm."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::settlement.payment","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e26","v141-b-g01-E02"],"rationale":"The same source paragraph states that the activation cost in aggregator bids is determined by clearing and that the DSO bears the activation fee; the payment source additionally specifies the standby and activation components and the branch in which only the standby price is paid when activation does not occur. The two chains express fee formation and payment obligations separately; only an assembly linkage is established here, without adding a C scientific edge from pricing to settlement."}],"annotation_policy":"Original D connections are annotations, not additional S edges.","empty_after_chain_suppression":false});
